                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Shawn McCarney",
                        "email": "shawnmm@us.ibm.com",
                        "username": "smccarney"
                    },
                    "message": "Note: I don't have this implemented yet, but the phosphor-power-sequencer application is going to be publishing both the system power state and the individual chassis power states on D-Bus.\n\nAny place in the phosphor-power-supply code where it checks the power state, you'll need to determine whether you should be looking at the **system** power state, or the **chassis** power state.\n\nFor example, if this chassis is in hardware isolation (guarded), it will not be powered on when the system is powered on.  So the system power state would be on, but this chassis's power state would be off.\n\nYou don't have to make these changes now, but make a note that this work is **required** to support multi-chassis eventually."
                },
